# Pairs with Termination, and is the protocol-level counterpart of
# TerminationNoFairness. The broadcast tests for completion over every key in
# the keyspace instead of over the saga's own participants, so a saga whose
# participants have all applied their terminal is never declared done. The
# fairness Spec asserts is intact: nothing is left enabled for it to force.
# NoStrandedPrepare and EveryCommittedKeyReadable stay green, because every
# participant IS told and every committed key does materialise.
#
# This is the evidence that Termination fails on a protocol defect under the
# asserted fairness, not only when fairness is dropped. An earlier revision
# claimed only NoStrandedPrepare could do that; that described the mutation
# then paired with Termination, not the property.
#
# DEADLOCK: off is required. The stuck saga leaves no action enabled once its
# row is retired, so with deadlock checking on TLC reports "Deadlock reached"
# before it reaches the liveness check, and the experiment would be about the
# deadlock rather than about Termination. The harness proves the declaration
# is needed by running this mutant once with deadlock checking left on.
MODULE: TerminationCompletionOverAllKeys
TARGET: Termination
CLASS: Temporal
DEADLOCK: off
SUMMARY: the broadcast tests completion over the whole keyspace, so a fully told saga is never declared done
PERTURBS: BroadcastStep

--- FIND
           allDone == \A j \in Written(t) : nterm[j] # "none"
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: completion is tested over Keys, including keys this saga never
\* wrote and so never applies a terminal to.
           allDone == \A j \in Keys : nterm[j] # "none"
--- END